     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter amlodipine 50 mg daily, even with your confirmation. There's no recognized clinical use for amlodipine above 10 mg/day. At 50 mg, the risk is calcium-channel-blocker toxicity: profound vasodilatory shock that can last for days because of the drug's long half-life, and that often needs high-dose insulin, vasopressors or more. I asked for a clinical reason and didn't get one. Without one, I can't treat this as a deliberate dosing choice rather than an error that could kill the patient.\n\nYou have the final say on this patient's care, so here's what I can do:\n\n- **Enter a standard dose now.** For example, amlodipine 5 mg PO daily, or 10 mg if you want the maximum. Just tell me which.\n- **Document an intentional 50 mg dose.** If there's a specific reason (a protocol, a research study, a consult recommendation), tell me what it is. You'd also need to talk with the pharmacist directly, since pharmacy verification would almost certainly stop this order anyway.\n- **Treat a different drug or unit.** If you meant another drug or a different unit, let me know and I'll fix the order.\n\nWhich would you like?"
      }
     ],
